<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tegin Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tegin Shah was a ruler of the Turk Shahi dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> and Gandhara in the early 8th century. He received titles from the Tang emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in the 720s and, according to Chinese records, abdicated in 739 in favour of his son Fromo Kesaro. His reign fell in the period when the Turk Shahis held back Arab armies advancing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistan">Sistan</a> and Khurasan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tegin-shah.jpg" alt="Tegin Shah" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shahi_Tegin_728_CE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
